t.io-parser and engine.io-parser vectors, the connection and socket cases of socket.io-client and engine.io-client against Node servers, plus differential runs where the Node client and this client play the same scenario against one recording server (",[144,145,149],"a",{"href":146,"rel":147},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fs00d\u002Frust-socketio\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fcrates\u002Fsocketio-next\u002Ftests\u002Fconformance.rs",[148],"nofollow",[150,151,152],"code",{},"crates\u002Fsocketio-next\u002Ftests\u002Fconformance.rs",").",[135,155,157],{"id":156},"not-implemented","Not implemented",[140,159,160],{},"On purpose:",[162,163,164,175,181,199,202,205,208,211,214],"ul",{},[165,166,167,168,171,172,174],"li",{},"one ",[150,169,170],{},"Manager"," multiplexing several namespaces over one connection (each ",[150,173,28],{}," has its own; connect several);",[165,176,177,180],{},[150,178,179],{},"volatile"," (offline emits already fail fast);",[165,182,183,186,187,190,191,194,195,198],{},[150,184,185],{},"retries"," \u002F ",[150,188,189],{},"ackTimeout"," queues, ",[150,192,193],{},"onAnyOutgoing",", ",[150,196,197],{},"forceBase64",";",[165,200,201],{},"WebTransport, WASM, Engine.IO v3 (socket.io 2.x servers), permessage-deflate;",[165,203,204],{},"the msgpack parser (a feature later if a server needs it);",[165,206,207],{},"derive macros for events;",[165,209,210],{},"concurrent handler dispatch (handlers run in order);",[165,212,213],{},"injecting your own reqwest or tungstenite client (it would tie the public API to their versions);",[165,215,216],{},"browser-only options.",[140,218,219,222],{},[150,220,221],{},"connect()"," returns the first attempt's error instead of retrying silently.",[135,224,226],{"id":225},"other-rust-clients","Other Rust clients",[140,228,229,234,235,238,239,242],{},[144,230,233],{"href":231,"rel":232},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002F1c3t3a\u002Frust-socketio",[148],"rust_socketio"," 0.6 is where this crate started (see the ",[144,23